  "body": "Follow-up of #2265.\n\nThe fix for #2265 adds a rule to `pass_link` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/ladder_links.rs`). When the user asks for a helix, ramp or arc entry, a pass start in material gets that entry, or a named stand-in. Only the pocket family (Pocket, rest 2D, Adaptive) opts in, through `Motion::with_solid_restart()` in `pocket_emit.rs`.\n\nThe other planar ladders (2D contour, slot, trace) do not opt in. Their pass starts use the existing entry laws.\n\nTo find:\n- Can a contour, slot or trace ladder start a pass (not the first pass of a level) in material with a centre-cutting tool, when the user asked for a helix or ramp?\n- If yes, file it as a defect by the AGENTS.md priority table, and opt that ladder in with its own pinning test and golden review.\n\nDone means: each planar ladder either opts in, or a test shows that its pass starts in material do not occur.\n",
